---
import Subpage from "../layouts/Subpage.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<Subpage
  title="Privacy: unflub collects nothing"
  description="unflub runs offline. No account, no telemetry, no analytics. What the app and this website do and do not collect, in plain words."
  crumb="Privacy"
>
  <h1>We collect nothing.</h1>
  <p class="lead">unflub runs on your computer and keeps to itself. This page says exactly what that means.</p>

  <h2>The app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Corrections are decided on your computer. unflub never sends what you type anywhere.</li>
    <li>
      It only holds the word you are typing, and the one before it for context, in memory. Nothing you type is written to disk.
    </li>
    <li>There is no account, no telemetry, no analytics and no advertising ID.</li>
    <li>
      Password fields are always skipped. Terminals and password managers are on the skip list from the start, and you can add
      any other app.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your settings, your words and your shortcuts are saved in a file on your computer. Uninstalling unflub removes the app;
      you can delete that file at any time.
    </li>
    <li>
      To tell you about a new version, unflub asks GitHub for the latest release. That request carries nothing you typed and no
      identifier.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    unflub.rmgn.ca sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts. It is served by Cloudflare, which handles each
    request (including your IP address) to deliver the page and protect the site from abuse. Download links point to GitHub,
    which has its own privacy statement.
  </p>

  <h2>Check for yourself</h2>
  <p>
    unflub is open source, so you do not have to take our word for any of this. <a href={SITE.repo}>Read the code on GitHub</a>,
    or <a href={SITE.issues}>open an issue</a> if you have a question.
  </p>

  <p class="small updated">Last updated November 2026. unflub is an <a href={SITE.org.url}>RMGN</a> product.</p>
</Subpage>

<style>
  .updated {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
</style>
